{"date":"2026-10-18","caps":[[0.05,"Arnie Jordan here, coming to you from row three at Jordan Arena, with the Rinkside Report."],[5.25,"Welcome back to both of my listeners."],[7.42,"It was Sunday, October eighteenth, and after a week off I showed up with a fresh notebook, two sharpened pencils and a large coffee."],[15.01,"I left with half a notebook, one pencil, and a napkin covered in arrows."],[19.18,"Thirty goals, three games, and two of them won by a single goal."],[23.54,"The early game was the Regatta Nordiques against the Culp Habs, and Fissel scored forty-five seconds in, set up by Regular."],[30.45,"Hunt tied it for the Habs, then Regular scored one himself late in the first, and another in the second, from Brophy and DeBolster."],[37.8,"With a name like Regular, you'd expect a regular night. Two goals and an assist? I'd call it premium."],[44.11,"The rest of that second period was a parade to the penalty box."],[47.69,"Brophy went for hooking, Paul went for tripping, and DeBolster went for something the timekeeper wrote down so fast I couldn't read it from row three."],[56.12,"Two Nordiques in the box in one period, and the Habs didn't score on either one."],[60.64,"Somewhere in there a clearing attempt went so high I lost it in the lights."],[64.89,"I believe it came down during the second game. I did not see who shot it, and I have decided not to find out."],[71.68,"Paul made up for his trip early in the third, making it three to two, but Moorzy and Fissel answered a minute and a half apart, with Roy setting up both."],[79.91,"Hunt got his second, and that's how it ended, five to three Nordiques."],[83.7,"Paul had a goal, two assists and a trip to the box, which in this league is what we call a full evening."],[89.31,"Trigg went the distance and held the Habs to three."],[92.73,"Game two was the Timbit Senators against the Keg Canucks, and I started a tally of lead changes on my napkin."],[98.66,"Davies scored late in the first, and Buynink stopped everything in that period, then handed the net to Shannon."],[104.7,"One perfect period, and the rest of the night off."],[108.08,"Then came the second period, and I am still recovering. Seven goals."],[111.86,"Williams went to the box for hooking ten seconds in. Ten seconds. I was still blowing on my coffee."],[117.34,"Obie made it two nothing, and then the Canucks scored three in a little over three minutes: Pundy, Adam Short, and Leyenhorst."],[124.29,"The Senators came back with Sheridan and Davies again, and Leyenhorst got his second to tie it at four."],[129.99,"Around goal number six, my first pencil snapped clean in half."],[134.07,"Martin put the Canucks ahead to start the third, with a goal and three assists on the night."],[139.06,"That's two leads for the Canucks, and they gave both of them back, which is very generous."],[143.94,"Obie tied it, and Schmidt scored the winner all by himself, no assists, didn't ask anybody."],[148.88,"Six to five Senators."],[150.06,"And then, with forty-seven seconds left and his team down by one, Pundy went to the box for interference."],[155.74,"Best seat in the house for the finish, I'll give him that. Better than row three."],[160.14,"Murphy had three helpers, and Shannon gave up five and still got the win."],[164.77,"The late game was Dawson's Oilers and the ColdBreak Leafs, and it turned into a hat trick contest."],[170.44,"Foran scored fifty-seven seconds in, then Horton and Grossi traded goals all first period."],[175.65,"NoPants and Grossi made it four to two Oilers in the second, before Adams and Pierce tied it right back up."],[181.83,"Then, halfway through the period, both teams changed goalies at the same moment."],[186.47,"Raimondo and Mallet out, Dawson and Rosie in. I thought it was a fire drill."],[190.88,"Rosie had been in net for exactly one minute when Grossi scored his third. Welcome to the game."],[197.01,"In the third, Misek went to the box for tripping, and forty-five seconds later Horton finished his own hat trick to tie it at five."],[204.0,"Then McPherson scored the winner, unassisted, with five thirty-six left. Last week he had six points."],[209.39,"This week he had one, and it was the one that counted. Grossi finished with five points."],[214.1,"Horton and Pierce had four each, and the Leafs got nothing for it but a sore neck from watching the scoreboard."],[220.68,"So that's your week: thirty goals, two hat tricks, two six to five finishes, and a napkin with four lead changes on it, every one of them from game two."],[228.94,"If I got your name wrong, or gave your goal to the fella beside you, take it up with the refs, the timekeeper, and how fast you people move out there."],[237.1,"Tape your sticks, and wave if you see me in row three. This has been Arnie Jordan with the Rinkside Report."]],"pages":[["ROW 3 - 10/18","!coffee spill (again)","pens: running dry","page getting full","pencil broke"],["G1: Nordiques @ Habs","Nordiques 3 - Habs 1","Fissel 2G!!","Regular 2G 1A!!","Hunt 2G!!"],["Nordiques 4 - Habs 2","!Brophy: hooking","KP 1G 2A","!DeBolster: too many men","need more pens"],["Nordiques 5 - Habs 3  FINAL","KP 1G 2A","Fissel 2G!!","Roy: 2 assists","Hunt 2G!!"],["G2: Sens @ Canucks","Sens 1 - Canucks 0","Davies 2G 1A!!","goalie change: Buynink","Shannon in net (swap)"],["Sens 4 - Canucks 4","!Williams: hooking","Obie 2G!!","Pundy 1G 1A","Short 1G"],["Sens 6 - Canucks 5  FINAL","New Guy 1G 3A","Obie 2G!!","Schmidt 1G","Pundy 1G 1A"],["G3: Oilers @ Leafs","Oilers 2 - Leafs 1","Dawson in net (swap)","Foran 1G 3A","Horton: 3 goals - HATS!"],["Oilers 6 - Leafs 5  FINAL","!Misek: tripping","Horton: 3 goals - HATS!","McPherson 1G","Grossi: 3 goals - HATS!"],["THAT'S THE WEEK","HAT TRICK - hats!","note: buy more pens","Tape your sticks!"]],"sleeper":{"team":"MTL","seed":5692},"kf":[{"t":23.54,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":1200,"h":0,"a":0,"goal":null,"final":false},{"t":27.33,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":1155,"h":0,"a":1,"goal":"FISSEL","final":false},{"t":30.45,"g":0,"pe